The Lead Autonomous Architect has completed the CSS layout audit and resolved the overlapping bunching bugs.

---

### 🚨 Layout Collision Diagnosis & Resolutions

#### 1. Title Container wrapping (`qms_manual_index.html`)
- **The Issue:** The main title and compliance indicators were locked within a rigid flexbox layout without wrapping parameters. On narrower screens, the title text and status badges collided on the same line, creating an unprofessional, bunched layout.
- **Resolution:** Refactored the title container in [`app/templates/qms_manual_index.html`](file:///file:///home/humbertoed/hexgrowth/app/templates/qms_manual_index.html) to support `flex-wrap: wrap` with a `1.5rem` gap and introduced a subtle bottom border division to structure the header.

#### 2. Grid Squeezing (Responsive CSS Breakpoints in `sop_base.html`)
- **The Issue:** The layout grid was configured as `1fr 280px` (where `280px` is the right Table of Contents column) alongside the fixed left navigation rail (`320px`). On viewports under 1400px, the remaining width for the document card was severely restricted, causing internal elements to collapse together.
- **Resolution:** Authored responsive CSS media query rules in [`app/templates/sop_base.html`](file:///home/humbertoed/hexgrowth/app/templates/sop_base.html):
  - **Viewports < 1400px:** Hides the right-side Table of Contents panel, collapses the grid layout to a single column (`1fr`), and reduces the padding of the card from `4rem` to `3rem`, immediately expanding the usable horizontal space.
  - **Viewports < 1024px (Mobile/Tablet):** Collapses the fixed left navigation rail (`320px`) to flow inline at the top of the viewport, granting the document card the full screen width.

---

### 📡 Staged Responsive Logic (`sop_base.html`)

The following responsive styles have been appended to the master QMS layout style definitions:

```css
